\name{gtheory_drug_review}
\alias{gtheory_drug_review}
\alias{drug_review}
\alias{drug_review_4aspect}
\docType{data}
\title{Synthetic Drug-Review Sentiment and Aspect Examples}
\description{Two toy outcome sets for five-category holistic sentiment and
four three-category aspects. All observations are synthetic; they are not
patient records, real review annotations, actual LLM outputs, or observations
from the cited drug-review corpus.}
\format{Each call to \code{\link{gt_example}} returns a list with a 576-row
\code{data} frame. Shared factors identify 24 hypothetical items, three generic
evaluators, two prompts, two temperature settings, and two seed identifiers.
Their levels are documented in the \link[=gtheory_datasets]{dataset overview}.
\describe{
\item{drug_review}{One ordered \code{score} under native coding:
1 = VERY_NEGATIVE, 2 = NEGATIVE, 3 = NEUTRAL, 4 = POSITIVE,
5 = VERY_POSITIVE. These category names represent holistic sentiment.}
\item{drug_review_4aspect}{Four outcome columns: \code{efficacy},
\code{safety}, \code{burden}, and \code{cost}. Each is ordered
NEGATIVE, NEUTRAL, POSITIVE under native coding.}
}
Native families are ordinal with probit links. The legacy
\code{coding = "manuscript"} option returns numerical Gaussian working scores:
1--5 for holistic sentiment and 1--3 for aspects. Other list elements identify
outcomes, families, design roles, coding, resource path, notes, and synthetic
provenance.}
\details{
The names illustrate four possible dimensions of review sentiment: treatment
effectiveness (efficacy), tolerability (safety), ease of use (burden), and
affordability (cost). The toy values were generated by integer arithmetic
without reading reviews or evaluating treatments. NEUTRAL is simply the middle
simulated category; it does not record an unmentioned aspect, missing response,
or patient's stated opinion. Aspects can differ from holistic sentiment.

The two sets share a hypothetical design and are not independent empirical
samples. Numeric-score compatibility treats category steps as equally spaced;
it retrieves no manuscript data or findings. No source ratings, drug names,
clinical outcomes, review text, actual model outputs, prevalence statistics,
or fitted parameters are included. Inspect \code{\link{gt_preflight}} before
fitting the intended source model; a 576-row table can still exceed dense
discrete dimension limits.
}
